## Third-party attributions

The packs below adapt published methods or prompts. The adaptations are original
Nuko Technologies LLC text under MIT; credit for the underlying work belongs to
its authors.

- packs/stair-toc-retrieval: method from Vineet Kumar, Meghanadh Pulivarthi,
  Vishwajeet Kumar, Jaydeep Sen, Riyaz Ahmad Bhat and Sachindra Joshi (IBM
  Research), "STAIR (STructure Aware Information Retriever): A novel dataset and
  LLM based retriever for document structure augmentation", arXiv:2609.03874
  (2026), https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.03874. The SearchTome benchmark is theirs.
  The pack is a prompt-level pattern; it does not include IBM's model weights,
  code or dataset. Licensed CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This pack is an original
  prompt-level adaptation of the method. Changes: the paper's model weights,
  code, and dataset are not included.

- packs/five-step-process-algorithm: inspired by the post by AI Guides
  (@free_ai_guides) on X, 7 October 2026, https://x.com/free_ai_guides, which
  applies Elon Musk's five-step algorithm. The pack text and prompt are original
  wording; only the idea is credited.

- packs/feynman-method: original Nuko Technologies LLC text implementing the
  widely shared Feynman learning method (simple explanation, confusion check,
  refinement cycles, application test, teaching snapshot), popularly associated
  with Richard P. Feynman. A public example of a similar skill, cited only as an
  example of the method and not as source text copied into this pack, is
  https://github.com/liza-mas/liza/blob/main/skills/feynman/SKILL.md (Apache-2.0).

